  "result": "The plan for `click.KeyValue` is ready at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-parsed-cray.md`. Nothing has been changed or run yet. I couldn't submit it for approval the usual way because that tool isn't available in this session, so please review it here.\n\n**The new type** goes in `src/click/types.py`, right after the existing UUID type, and follows the same pattern:\n- It splits the input at the first `=`, so `a=b=c` becomes `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`.\n- An empty value is allowed (`a=` becomes `(\"a\", \"\")`).\n- Input with no `=`, or with an empty key, fails with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- A value that is already a 2-tuple, such as a default, is passed through unchanged.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- **Export:** add `KeyValue` to the imports in `src/click/__init__.py` so `click.KeyValue` works.\n- **Docs:** add `KeyValue` to `docs/parameter-types.md` and `docs/api.md`, plus an entry in `CHANGES.md` under a new 8.6.0 version.\n- **Tests (`tests/test_types.py`):**\n  - inputs that should parse;\n  - inputs that should fail (`ab`, `=b`, empty string), checking for exit code 2 and the error message;\n  - a `multiple=True` option.\n- **Verification:** run `uv run pytest`.\n\nLet me know if you approve, or want changes (for example, trimming whitespace around the key or value), and I'll implement it.",
